# Held-out validation plan

Prepared before the corrected 60-case discovery map is complete. This is a private
planning document, not a result or an authorization to begin native execution.

The discovery bank reuses four observed schools. After its complete physical,
source, accounting and exact-anchor audits pass, select the dolphin-only herding
minimum H0 with the largest mean 36T dolphin catch across those four schools.
Break ties by smaller H. Select the mixed setting (H*, N*) with the largest mean
dolphin catch minus the selected H0 dolphin-only mean, across all nine mixed
settings. Break ties by fewer gannets, then smaller H. Record every cell and the
gannet response; a favourable gannet sign is not a selection requirement. Freeze
H0, H*, N*, all source hashes, discovery seals and the selection table before any
held-out feeding step. Do not change this rule after seeing held-out outcomes.

Use eight fresh candidate school seeds 39065501 through 39065508, capture setting
61001, 160 fish and the same original preparation algorithm. Preserve the 20T
burn-in, original 36T predator-free stability screen and additional 36T route
diagnostic used for the prior independent cohort. The original inclusion criteria
apply only to the original 36T screen. Keep every candidate disposition; no seed
replacement or screening against feeding outcomes. A rejected preparation pauses
execution for a recorded technical review; it is never silently replaced. The
same saved 20T school and stable-ID predator/private-stream starts are paired
across conditions and numerical grids.

Primary experiment: fine dt=0.000625, 36T, on all accepted held-out schools.
Conditions are D(H*), DG(H*, N*), G-only(N*) and D(H0) when H0 differs from H*.
The primary estimand is the paired dolphin catch-rate difference DG minus D(H*)
over the full encounter, captures/(12*36). Report raw catches and the mean paired
absolute difference alongside the rate. The fixed H0 comparison and per-bird
DG-minus-G-only difference are secondary. Do not reselect H0 on held-out schools.

Secondary numerical comparison: coarse dt=0.00125, 36T, D(H*) and DG(H*, N*) on
the same eight saved schools. Report fine and coarse outcomes side by side, their
school-level signs and paired fine-minus-coarse change. Do not call agreement a
proof of convergence or disagreement evidence that one physical mechanism is
false. No 72T extension, parameter expansion, new probability or model alteration
is included in this plan.

The independent sampling unit is a starting school. Use one common whole-school
bootstrap index matrix (10,000 draws, NumPy PCG64 seed 88495509) for paired mean
differences and pointwise 95% percentile intervals. All eight school outcomes and
accepted/rejected counts remain visible. The single primary endpoint is distinct
from secondary species and numerical diagnostics. School and grid repetitions
are not independent samples. Do not pool discovery and held-out estimates.

Maximum preparation budget: 8*(20+72)/0.00125 = 588,800 native steps.
Maximum fine feeding budget: 8*4*36/0.000625 = 1,843,200 steps (three conditions
if H0=H*). Secondary coarse budget: 8*2*36/0.00125 = 460,800 steps.
The largest full-study ceiling is 2,892,800 native steps, before any explicitly
bounded integration smoke. At most three feeding workers, one numerical thread
per worker; never overlap two unrestricted feeding ensembles. Store fresh outputs
with regular heartbeat and sufficient disk reserve. Preserve failed attempts.

Gates: complete discovery map and independent audit; frozen deterministic
selection; source/input/initial-state review; bounded smoke with unchanged
physical/accounting/RNG checks; recorded execution approval; full run; independent
evidence review. The existing native binary, dolphin rules, gannet rules, q=.7,
point contact, depth/turning/speed constraints and fixed three-site nested bird
roster remain unchanged. New binary builds belong to software portability checks,
not to this scientific comparison. A completed run is published regardless of
effect sign. No success-based stopping, reruns, seed replacement or threshold
adjustments are allowed.
